#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0240_000_0
#. timeline 2368..3037
#: codec/1/157/0x9d5c0/2
msgid ""
"While he was there, he visited Hiroshima.\n"
msgstr ""
"期间他去了广岛。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0240_000_0
#. timeline 3037..3301
#: codec/1/157/0x9d5c0/3
msgid ""
"Hiroshima...\n"
msgstr ""
"广岛……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0240_000_0
#. timeline 3329..4137
#: codec/1/157/0x9d5c0/4
msgid ""
"Since he was there to discuss economic issues,\n"
msgstr ""
"他去那儿是谈经济问题，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0240_000_0
#. timeline 4207..5057
#: codec/1/157/0x9d5c0/5
msgid ""
"Hiroshima wasn't part of the original itinerary.\n"
msgstr ""
"广岛本不在原定行程里。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0240_000_0
#. timeline 5126..6631
#: codec/1/157/0x9d5c0/6
msgid ""
"Some said the Ministry of Foreign Affairs didn't\n"
"want to let him go. But he went anyway.\n"
msgstr ""
"有人说外交部不想放他走。\n"
"但他还是去了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0240_000_0
#. timeline 6687..7578
#: codec/1/157/0x9d5c0/7
msgid ""
"He snuck out of his hotel and took an overnight\n"
"train.\n"
msgstr ""
"他偷偷溜出酒店，乘坐了一夜\n"
"火车。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0240_000_0
#. timeline 7829..8930
#: codec/1/157/0x9d5c0/8
msgid ""
"Traveling guerrilla-style - sounds like Che, all right.\n"
msgstr ""
"游击式出行——确实是切。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0240_000_0
#. timeline 8958..10309
#: codec/1/157/0x9d5c0/9
msgid ""
"He visited the Peace Memorial Museum and the\n"
"Atomic Bomb Survivors Hospital.\n"
msgstr ""
"他参观了和平纪念博物馆和\n"
"原子弹幸存者医院。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0240_000_0
#. timeline 10421..10992
#: codec/1/157/0x9d5c0/10
msgid ""
"Apparently it gave him quite a shock.\n"
msgstr ""
"据说他深受震撼。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0240_000_0
#. timeline 11020..12204
#: codec/1/157/0x9d5c0/11
msgid ""
"As a doctor, it must have been painful for him to\n"
"see how the victims suffered.\n"
msgstr ""
"作为一名医生，看到受害者遭受的痛苦，\n"
"他一定很难受。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0240_000_0
#. timeline 12232..12733
#: codec/1/157/0x9d5c0/12
msgid ""
"Nukes destroy everything...\n"
msgstr ""
"核弹摧毁一切……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0240_000_0
#. timeline 12747..13123
#: codec/1/157/0x9d5c0/13
msgid ""
"He was quoted as saying,\n"
msgstr ""
"他原话是，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0240_000_0
#. timeline 13263..14475
#: codec/1/157/0x9d5c0/14
msgid ""
"\"They put you through this, and still you do\n"
"whatever America says?\"\n"
msgstr ""
"“他们让你经历这些，你还\n"
"对美国言听计从？”\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0240_000_0
#. timeline 14531..15743
#: codec/1/157/0x9d5c0/15
msgid ""
"...Those words really hit me hard. Especially when I\n"
"think of my mom.\n"
msgstr ""
"……那些话真刺痛了我。尤其当我\n"
"想到妈妈。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0240_000_0
#. timeline 15770..17261
#: codec/1/157/0x9d5c0/16
msgid ""
"He said something else, too: \"Let us all love\n"
"Hiroshima, and its people.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"他还说：“让我们都爱\n"
"广岛和它的人民。”\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0240_000_0
#. timeline 17303..18752
#: codec/1/157/0x9d5c0/17
msgid ""
"I can believe it. Che never managed to numb\n"
"himself to other people's pain.\n"
msgstr ""
"我相信。切始终没能让自己对他人的痛苦\n"
"变得麻木。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0240_000_0
#. timeline 18975..20089
#: codec/1/157/0x9d5c0/18
msgid ""
"That's why people loved him. And why he died.\n"
msgstr ""
"所以人们爱他。所以他死了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0260_000_0
#. timeline 487..1574
#: codec/1/157/0x9dc70/0
msgid ""
"That bandanna you're always wearing - that thing's\n"
"a real antique.\n"
msgstr ""
"你一直戴的那条头巾，那玩意儿\n"
"可是真古董。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0260_000_0
#. timeline 1657..2131
#: codec/1/157/0x9dc70/1
msgid ""
"Ever think about getting a new one?\n"
msgstr ""
"没想过换条新的？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0260_000_0
#. timeline 2145..2563
#: codec/1/157/0x9dc70/2
msgid ""
"This one's fine.\n"
msgstr ""
"这条挺好。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0260_000_0
#. timeline 2577..3636
#: codec/1/157/0x9dc70/3
msgid ""
"Come on, we can't have our Boss wearing a\n"
"raggedy old thing like that...\n"
msgstr ""
"拜托，咱老大可不能戴\n"
"那么破旧的东西……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0260_000_0
#. timeline 3636..5057
#: codec/1/157/0x9dc70/4
msgid ""
"It was a gift, OK? It wouldn't be right to get rid of\n"
"it.\n"
msgstr ""
"那是礼物，行吗？把它扔掉\n"
"不合适。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0260_000_0
#. timeline 5071..6060
#: codec/1/157/0x9dc70/5
msgid ""
"It was? OK, then... Speaking of which,\n"
msgstr ""
"是吗？那行…说起来，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0260_000_0
#. timeline 6157..7133
#: codec/1/157/0x9dc70/6
msgid ""
"Che supposedly had a black scarf he used to take\n"
"everywhere with him.\n"
msgstr ""
"据说切有一条黑围巾，他以前走到哪儿\n"
"都带着。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0260_000_0
#. timeline 7133..7411
#: codec/1/157/0x9dc70/7
msgid ""
"A scarf?\n"
msgstr ""
"围巾?\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0260_000_0
#. timeline 7411..8303
#: codec/1/157/0x9dc70/8
msgid ""
"One of his comrades gave it to him when he broke\n"
"his arm in battle.\n"
msgstr ""
"他战斗中摔断手臂时，一位战友\n"
"把围巾给了他。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0260_000_0
#. timeline 8331..8986
#: codec/1/157/0x9dc70/9
msgid ""
"Che used that silk scarf as a sling...\n"
msgstr ""
"切拿那条丝巾当吊带……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0260_000_0
#. timeline 9083..10072
#: codec/1/157/0x9dc70/10
msgid ""
"and the comrade who gave it to him became his\n"
"second wife.\n"
msgstr ""
"给他围巾的战友后来成了他\n"
"第二任妻子。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0260_000_0
#. timeline 10086..10393
#: codec/1/157/0x9dc70/11
msgid ""
"Aleida, right?\n"
msgstr ""
"阿蕾达？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0260_000_0
#. timeline 10421..11591
#: codec/1/157/0x9dc70/12
msgid ""
"Even after his arm healed up, he never went\n"
"anywhere without that scarf.\n"
msgstr ""
"手臂痊愈后，他也从未\n"
"不带那条围巾出门。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0260_000_0
#. timeline 11619..12608
#: codec/1/157/0x9dc70/13
msgid ""
"What about you? You get that bandanna from\n"
"someone special?\n"
msgstr ""
"那你呢？头巾是\n"
"某个特别的人给的？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0260_000_0
#. timeline 12608..14182
#: codec/1/157/0x9dc70/14
msgid ""
"No, nothing like that. It's... important to me, that's all.\n"
msgstr ""
"不，不是。只是……对我很重要。\n"

#: codec/1/158/0x9e190/0
msgid ""
"You were saying Japan has a peace constitution,\n"
"too?\n"
msgstr ""
"你刚才说日本也有和平宪法，\n"
"对吧？\n"

#: codec/1/158/0x9e190/1
msgid ""
"Yep. Japan renounced war in Article 9 of its\n"
"constitution.\n"
msgstr ""
"是的。日本宪法第九条\n"
"放弃了战争。\n"

#: codec/1/158/0x9e190/2
msgid ""
"Aspiring sincerely to an international peace based\n"
"on justice and order...\n"
msgstr ""
"真诚地渴望基于正义与秩序\n"
"的国际和平……\n"

#: codec/1/158/0x9e190/3
msgid ""
"...the Japanese people forever renounce war as a\n"
"sovereign right of the nation\n"
msgstr ""
"……日本人民永远放弃以国家主权\n"
"发动战争的权利\n"

#: codec/1/158/0x9e190/4
msgid ""
"and the threat or use of force as means of\n"
"settling international disputes.\n"
msgstr ""
"以及以武力威胁或行使武力\n"
"作为解决国际争端的手段。\n"

#: codec/1/158/0x9e190/5
msgid ""
"In order to accomplish the aim of the preceding\n"
"paragraph,\n"
msgstr ""
"为了实现前款\n"
"所述之目的，\n"

#: codec/1/158/0x9e190/6
msgid ""
"land, sea, and air forces, as well as other war\n"
"potential, will never be maintained.\n"
msgstr ""
"陆、海、空力量以及其他战争\n"
"潜力，将永不保持。\n"

#: codec/1/158/0x9e190/7
msgid ""
"The right of belligerency of the state will not be\n"
"recognized.\n"
msgstr ""
"国家的交战权将不被\n"
"承认。\n"

#: codec/1/158/0x9e190/8
msgid ""
"You know it by heart?\n"
msgstr ""
"你背下来了？\n"

#: codec/1/158/0x9e190/9
msgid ""
"Some things you never forget.\n"
msgstr ""
"有些事永远忘不了。\n"

#: codec/1/158/0x9e190/10
msgid ""
"Impressive. There were some parts I didn't quite\n"
"get, though\n"
msgstr ""
"令人印象深刻。不过有些部分我\n"
"不太明白\n"

#: codec/1/158/0x9e190/11
msgid ""
"- like the whole \"means of settling conflicts\" thing.\n"
msgstr ""
"比如“解决争端的手段”那句。\n"

#: codec/1/158/0x9e190/12
msgid ""
"Yeah, that's been the subject of debate.\n"
msgstr ""
"对，这一直有争议。\n"

#: codec/1/158/0x9e190/13
msgid ""
"Whether or not it forbids any and all use of force.\n"
msgstr ""
"是否禁止一切武力使用。\n"

#: codec/1/158/0x9e190/14
msgid ""
"The current constitution was originally drawn up\n"
"under the Allied occupation.\n"
msgstr ""
"现行宪法最初是在盟军占领下\n"
"制定的。\n"

#: codec/1/158/0x9e190/15
msgid ""
"The first draft was even submitted by Allied GHQ.\n"
msgstr ""
"初稿甚至是盟军总司令部提交的。\n"

#: codec/1/158/0x9e190/16
msgid ""
"So naturally there are some who feel the\n"
"constitution was imposed on Japan by foreigners.\n"
msgstr ""
"所以自然有人觉得，宪法是\n"
"外国人强加给日本的。\n"

#: codec/1/158/0x9e190/17
msgid ""
"Things like that are never simple. Same for every\n"
"country, I guess...\n"
msgstr ""
"这种事从来都不简单。\n"
"大概每个国家都一样……\n"

#: codec/1/158/0x9e190/18
msgid ""
"One thing's for sure, though\n"
msgstr ""
"不过有一点可以肯定\n"

#: codec/1/158/0x9e190/19
msgid ""
"- not having an army let Japan focus on economic\n"
"recovery after the war.\n"
msgstr ""
"——没有军队让日本战后能专注\n"
"经济复兴。\n"

#: codec/1/158/0x9e190/20
msgid ""
"In that sense, it's the same as Costa Rica.\n"
msgstr ""
"这么说，和哥斯达黎加一样。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0300_010_0
#. timeline 473..1407
#: codec/1/158/0x9e950/0
msgid ""
"Kaz, you were in the Japanese Self-Defense Force,\n"
"right?\n"
msgstr ""
"卡兹，你以前在日本自卫队待过，\n"
"对吧？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0300_010_0
#. timeline 1462..2117
#: codec/1/158/0x9e950/1
msgid ""
"I thought that Article 9 you were talking about\n"
"earlier\n"
msgstr ""
"我之前听你说的那个第9条\n"
"来着\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0300_010_0
#. timeline 2117..2772
#: codec/1/158/0x9e950/2
msgid ""
"prevented Japan from having an army...\n"
msgstr ""
"让日本不能拥有军队……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0300_010_0
#. timeline 2786..3650
#: codec/1/158/0x9e950/3
msgid ""
"Yeah, and that's another subject of controversy.\n"
msgstr ""
"对，那也是个争议点。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0300_010_0
#. timeline 3678..4834
#: codec/1/158/0x9e950/4
msgid ""
"\"The Self-Defense Force is an organization for the\n"
"purpose of defense.\n"
msgstr ""
"“自卫队是以防卫为目的的\n"
"组织。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0300_010_0
#. timeline 4917..6199
#: codec/1/158/0x9e950/5
msgid ""
"Article 9 of the constitution does not deny Japan's\n"
"right to self-defense.\n"
msgstr ""
"宪法第九条并不否认日本的\n"
"自卫权。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0300_010_0
#. timeline 6339..7202
#: codec/1/158/0x9e950/6
msgid ""
"Therefore, the SDF is constitutional.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"因此，自卫队符合宪法。”\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0300_010_0
#. timeline 7244..7829
#: codec/1/158/0x9e950/7
msgid ""
"That's Tokyo's official stance.\n"
msgstr ""
"这是东京的官方立场。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0300_010_0
#. timeline 8108..8637
#: codec/1/158/0x9e950/8
msgid ""
"...Sounds complicated.\n"
msgstr ""
"……好复杂。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0300_010_0
#. timeline 8637..9877
#: codec/1/158/0x9e950/9
msgid ""
"Call it what you will, it's a distinctly Japanese way\n"
"of interpreting things.\n"
msgstr ""
"不管怎么说，这都是典型的日本式\n"
"解释方式。\n"

#: codec/1/158/0x9ecf0/0
msgid ""
"The U.S. has military forces stationed in Japan,\n"
"right?\n"
msgstr ""
"美国在日本驻有军队，\n"
"对吧？\n"

#: codec/1/158/0x9ecf0/1
msgid ""
"Right. Even though the Allied occupation ended,\n"
msgstr ""
"对。虽然盟军的占领已经结束，\n"

#: codec/1/158/0x9ecf0/2
msgid ""
"American forces are still stationed there under the\n"
"U.S.-Japan Security Treaty.\n"
msgstr ""
"但依据《日美安保条约》，\n"
"美军仍然驻扎在那里。\n"

#: codec/1/158/0x9ecf0/3
#: codec/1/182/0xb66e0/4
msgid ""
"Unlike Costa Rica.\n"
msgstr ""
"哥斯达黎加则不然。\n"

#: codec/1/158/0x9ecf0/4
msgid ""
"Part of it stems from the occupation,\n"
msgstr ""
"一部分源于当年的占领，\n"

#: codec/1/158/0x9ecf0/5
msgid ""
"but Japan also occupies a key strategic position\n"
"from America's perspective.\n"
msgstr ""
"但在美国看来，日本\n"
"还占据着关键的战略位置。\n"

#: codec/1/158/0x9ecf0/6
msgid ""
"It's next door to the Soviet Union, and close to\n"
"China and North Korea as well.\n"
msgstr ""
"它紧邻苏联，\n"
"也靠近中国和朝鲜。\n"

#: codec/1/158/0x9ecf0/7
msgid ""
"It's integral to the security of Pacific Asia.\n"
msgstr ""
"它是亚太安全不可或缺的一环。\n"

#: codec/1/158/0x9ecf0/8
msgid ""
"For America, Japan represents a barrier against\n"
"communism.\n"
msgstr ""
"对美国来说，日本是\n"
"抵挡共产主义的屏障。\n"

#: codec/1/158/0x9ecf0/9
msgid ""
"What about for Japan?\n"
msgstr ""
"那对日本呢？\n"

#: codec/1/158/0x9ecf0/10
msgid ""
"As you might expect, there's deep-rooted\n"
"opposition to the alliance.\n"
msgstr ""
"不出所料，反对这个同盟的\n"
"声音根深蒂固。\n"

#: codec/1/158/0x9ecf0/11
msgid ""
"In 1960 and 1970, when the treaty was up for\n"
"revision,\n"
msgstr ""
"1960年和1970年，条约面临\n"
"修订时，\n"

#: codec/1/158/0x9ecf0/12
msgid ""
"there were mass protest movements against it.\n"
msgstr ""
"爆发了大规模的抗议运动。\n"

#: codec/1/158/0x9ecf0/13
msgid ""
"Especially in Okinawa. The U.S. only gave it back to\n"
"Japan two years ago,\n"
msgstr ""
"尤其在冲绳。美国两年前\n"
"才把它归还日本，\n"

#: codec/1/158/0x9ecf0/14
msgid ""
"and American bases are still concentrated there.\n"
msgstr ""
"而美军基地至今仍集中在那里。\n"

#: codec/1/158/0x9ecf0/15
msgid ""
"It's a heavy burden for the Okinawans to bear.\n"
msgstr ""
"对冲绳人来说，这是沉重的负担。\n"

#: codec/1/158/0x9ecf0/16
msgid ""
"Then why don't they scrap the treaty?\n"
msgstr ""
"那为什么不干脆废掉条约？\n"

#: codec/1/158/0x9ecf0/17
msgid ""
"Lots of reasons. There's the imbalance of power\n"
"with the U.S., of course.\n"
msgstr ""
"原因很多。当然，首先是\n"
"与美国的力量失衡。\n"

#: codec/1/158/0x9ecf0/18
msgid ""
"And if Japan pulled out, they'd be losing the\n"
"nuclear umbrella America provides.\n"
msgstr ""
"而且日本一旦退出，就会\n"
"失去美国提供的核保护伞。\n"

#: codec/1/158/0x9ecf0/19
msgid ""
"And as for whether the JSDF could defend the\n"
"country after the Americans left...\n"
msgstr ""
"至于美军撤离后自卫队\n"
"能否守卫这个国家……\n"

#: codec/1/158/0x9ecf0/20
msgid ""
"I really couldn't say.\n"
msgstr ""
"我真的说不好。\n"

#: codec/1/158/0x9ecf0/21
msgid ""
"Costa Rica's in a similar situation.\n"
msgstr ""
"哥斯达黎加的处境相似。\n"

#: codec/1/158/0x9ecf0/22
msgid ""
"They depend on the Inter-American Treaty of\n"
"Reciprocal Assistance, the so-called Rio Pact.\n"
msgstr ""
"他们依赖《美洲国家互助条约》，\n"
"也就是所谓的里约条约。\n"

#: codec/1/158/0x9ecf0/23
msgid ""
"So the countries with peace constitutions\n"
msgstr ""
"所以那些有和平宪法的国家，\n"

#: codec/1/158/0x9ecf0/24
msgid ""
"end up having to rely on other countries' armies...\n"
"Kind of ironic.\n"
msgstr ""
"最后只能依赖别国的军队……\n"
"挺讽刺的。\n"

#: codec/1/158/0x9ecf0/25
msgid ""
"On the flip side, not everybody in America is\n"
"satisfied with it, either.\n"
msgstr ""
"反过来看，美国人里\n"
"也不是人人都满意。\n"

#: codec/1/158/0x9ecf0/26
msgid ""
"Some people argue Japan is freeloading off\n"
"America's security guarantee.\n"
msgstr ""
"有人认为日本在白蹭\n"
"美国的安全保障。\n"

#: codec/1/158/0x9ecf0/27
msgid ""
"And you know how Japan's industrial exports are\n"
"making inroads in the States.\n"
msgstr ""
"你也知道，日本的工业品\n"
"正在大举打进美国市场。\n"

#: codec/1/158/0x9ecf0/28
msgid ""
"Yeah. I've got a Japanese camera myself. Best\n"
"damn camera around.\n"
msgstr ""
"是啊。我自己就有台日本相机，\n"
"好得没话说。\n"

#: codec/1/158/0x9ecf0/29
msgid ""
"Japan's low defense spending allows it to invest\n"
"more in economic recovery\n"
msgstr ""
"日本军费低，就能把更多钱\n"
"投入经济复兴，\n"

#: codec/1/158/0x9ecf0/30
msgid ""
"and expand its share of the American market.\n"
msgstr ""
"进而扩大在美国市场的份额。\n"

#: codec/1/158/0x9ecf0/31
msgid ""
"That's a bitter pill for Americans to swallow.\n"
msgstr ""
"这口苦药美国人难以下咽。\n"

#: codec/1/159/0x9f870/0
msgid ""
"You know that today, Japan is under the American\n"
"nuclear umbrella...\n"
msgstr ""
"你知道如今日本处于美国的\n"
"核保护伞下……\n"

#: codec/1/159/0x9f870/2
msgid ""
"The U.S. vowed to retaliate against any country\n"
msgstr ""
"美国承诺会报复任何国家\n"

#: codec/1/159/0x9f870/3
msgid ""
"that launches a nuclear strike against an allied\n"
"country...\n"
msgstr ""
"那会对盟国发动核打击的\n"
"国家……\n"

#: codec/1/159/0x9f870/4
msgid ""
"That promise deters nuclear attacks against\n"
"America's allies.\n"
msgstr ""
"这一承诺威慑了对美国盟国的\n"
"核攻击。\n"

#: codec/1/159/0x9f870/5
msgid ""
"Hence the term \"nuclear umbrella.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"所以叫“核保护伞”。\n"

#: codec/1/159/0x9f870/6
msgid ""
"But suppose the Russians nuked Tokyo.\n"
msgstr ""
"但假设苏联用核弹打东京。\n"

#: codec/1/159/0x9f870/7
msgid ""
"Would America really nuke Moscow in return?\n"
msgstr ""
"美国真会核平莫斯科作为回击？\n"

#: codec/1/159/0x9f870/8
msgid ""
"If they did, the Soviet Union would undoubtedly\n"
"retaliate.\n"
msgstr ""
"若真如此，苏联必将\n"
"报复。\n"

#: codec/1/159/0x9f870/9
msgid ""
"Would Washington really be willing to risk\n"
msgstr ""
"华盛顿真愿冒险\n"

#: codec/1/159/0x9f870/10
msgid ""
"having a bomb dropped on itself in order to\n"
"avenge Japan?\n"
msgstr ""
"为向日本复仇，\n"
"不惜自己挨一颗炸弹？\n"

#: codec/1/159/0x9f870/11
msgid ""
"...I'm not so sure.\n"
msgstr ""
"…不确定。\n"

#: codec/1/159/0x9f870/12
msgid ""
"Don't tell me you're still worried about Japan. After\n"
"all these years?\n"
msgstr ""
"别告诉我你还在担心日本。都\n"
"这么多年了？\n"

#: codec/1/159/0x9f870/13
msgid ""
"It's not that. I just...\n"
msgstr ""
"不是那事。我只是……\n"

#: codec/1/159/0x9f870/14
msgid ""
"To be honest, I'm not convinced, either.\n"
msgstr ""
"说实话，我也不信。\n"

#: codec/1/159/0x9f870/15
msgid ""
"But Moscow faces the same dilemma. Maybe\n"
"Washington wouldn't retaliate on Japan's behalf.\n"
msgstr ""
"但莫斯科也面临同样困境。也许\n"
"华盛顿不会为日本报复。\n"

#: codec/1/159/0x9f870/16
msgid ""
"Then again, maybe it would.\n"
msgstr ""
"可也许它会。\n"

#: codec/1/159/0x9f870/17
msgid ""
"So you're saying Moscow wouldn't want to risk\n"
"being attacked, either...\n"
msgstr ""
"你是说莫斯科也不想冒\n"
"被攻击的风险……\n"

#: codec/1/159/0x9f870/18
msgid ""
"The whole concept of nuclear deterrence is\n"
"entirely hypothetical to begin with.\n"
msgstr ""
"核威慑这概念本身\n"
"就纯属假设。\n"

#: codec/1/159/0x9f870/19
msgid ""
"When you get down to it, it's all smoke and mirrors.\n"
msgstr ""
"说到底，全是虚张声势。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0320_000_0
#. timeline 487..2424
#: codec/1/159/0x9ff20/0
msgid ""
"\"Japan shall not possess, manufacture, or allow the\n"
"introduction of nuclear weapons into Japan\"...\n"
msgstr ""
"「日本不得拥有、制造核武器，\n"
"也不得允许其运入日本」……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0320_000_0
#. timeline 2577..3705
#: codec/1/159/0x9ff20/1
msgid ""
"Those are the Three Non-Nuclear Principles set\n"
"forth by the Japanese government.\n"
msgstr ""
"那是日本政府提出的\n"
"“无核三原则”。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0320_000_0
#. timeline 3733..4513
#: codec/1/159/0x9ff20/2
msgid ""
"\"Allow the introduction\"...? That's funny.\n"
msgstr ""
"“容许引进”……？真可笑。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0320_000_0
#. timeline 4681..5781
#: codec/1/159/0x9ff20/3
msgid ""
"Some of the U.S. warships that visit Japanese\n"
"ports are armed with nukes...\n"
msgstr ""
"停靠日本港口的美军舰艇里，\n"
"有些就装着核武器……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0320_000_0
#. timeline 5795..7007
#: codec/1/159/0x9ff20/4
msgid ""
"Or are you gonna tell me they transfer them at\n"
"sea onto other ships every time they visit?\n"
msgstr ""
"难不成你要说，每次停靠\n"
"都在海上把核弹转到别的船上？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0320_000_0
#. timeline 7021..8456
#: codec/1/159/0x9ff20/5
msgid ""
"You raise a good point, Snake. But the Japanese\n"
"government doesn't recognize it as such.\n"
msgstr ""
"说得好，斯内克。\n"
"但日本政府不这么认定。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0320_000_0
#. timeline 8470..9418
#: codec/1/159/0x9ff20/6
msgid ""
"The introduction of nuclear weapons into Japanese\n"
"territory\n"
msgstr ""
"把核武器运进\n"
"日本领土\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0320_000_0
#. timeline 9473..10866
#: codec/1/159/0x9ff20/7
msgid ""
"would need to be agreed upon in advance. America\n"
"hasn't made any such agreements.\n"
msgstr ""
"需要事先达成协议。\n"
"而美国没做过这种约定。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0320_000_0
#. timeline 10950..12385
#: codec/1/159/0x9ff20/8
msgid ""
"Therefore, they aren't bringing nukes into Japan....\n"
"That's the official excuse.\n"
msgstr ""
"所以他们没有把核武器带进日本……\n"
"这就是官方的托辞。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0320_000_0
#. timeline 12817..13555
#: codec/1/159/0x9ff20/9
msgid ""
"...Doesn't sound like much of an excuse to me.\n"
msgstr ""
"……我听着可不像什么托辞。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0320_000_0
#. timeline 13555..14976
#: codec/1/159/0x9ff20/10
msgid ""
"I don't blame you. Keep in mind, though, Japan's\n"
"suffered actual nuclear attacks.\n"
msgstr ""
"我不怪你。但别忘了，日本\n"
"真的挨过核打击。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0320_000_0
#. timeline 15074..15896
#: codec/1/159/0x9ff20/11
msgid ""
"Anti-nuke sentiment there runs deeper than you\n"
"think.\n"
msgstr ""
"那里的反核情绪，比你想的\n"
"更深。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0320_000_0
#. timeline 15924..17136
#: codec/1/159/0x9ff20/12
msgid ""
"I suppose the government's not really in a position\n"
"to admit that sort of thing.\n"
msgstr ""
"我想，政府也确实\n"
"没法承认这种事。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0330_000_0
#. timeline 473..1727
#: codec/1/160/0xa04e0/0
msgid ""
"So tell me, Kaz, how's the Self-Defense Force you\n"
"were in different from an army?\n"
msgstr ""
"那卡兹，你待过的自卫队\n"
"和军队有何不同？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0330_000_0
#. timeline 1727..2563
#: codec/1/160/0xa04e0/1
msgid ""
"The JSDF is set up for national defense.\n"
msgstr ""
"日本自卫队是为国防而设。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0330_000_0
#. timeline 2633..3566
#: codec/1/160/0xa04e0/2
msgid ""
"It's not configured for aggression against other\n"
"countries.\n"
msgstr ""
"并非为侵略他国\n"
"而配置。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0330_000_0
#. timeline 3636..4360
#: codec/1/160/0xa04e0/3
msgid ""
"It's what you'd call exclusive defense.\n"
msgstr ""
"就是所谓的专守防卫。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0330_000_0
#. timeline 4374..4834
#: codec/1/160/0xa04e0/4
msgid ""
"Exclusive... defense?\n"
msgstr ""
"专守……防卫？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0330_000_0
#. timeline 4834..6436
#: codec/1/160/0xa04e0/5
msgid ""
"It's the fundamental strategic posture of the JSDF.\n"
"No preemptive attacks.\n"
msgstr ""
"这是自卫队的根本战略姿态。\n"
"不发动先制攻击。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0330_000_0
#. timeline 6492..7648
#: codec/1/160/0xa04e0/6
msgid ""
"Only the minimum defensive action necessary after\n"
"an enemy attacks.\n"
msgstr ""
"只在遭敌攻击后采取\n"
"最低限度防御行动。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0330_000_0
#. timeline 7662..8400
#: codec/1/160/0xa04e0/7
msgid ""
"Anything defined as self defense, then.\n"
msgstr ""
"凡被界定为自卫的皆可。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0330_000_0
#. timeline 8414..9473
#: codec/1/160/0xa04e0/8
msgid ""
"The JSDF originated as the National Police Reserve.\n"
msgstr ""
"自卫队前身是警察预备队。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0330_000_0
#. timeline 9501..11020
#: codec/1/160/0xa04e0/9
msgid ""
"Back then, American forces stationed in Japan\n"
"were being sent over to fight in the Korean War.\n"
msgstr ""
"当时驻日美军\n"
"被派去参加朝鲜战争。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0330_000_0
#. timeline 11117..11939
#: codec/1/160/0xa04e0/10
msgid ""
"So in a sense, the NPR was filling a gap.\n"
msgstr ""
"所以警预队是在补缺。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0330_000_0
#. timeline 11981..13054
#: codec/1/160/0xa04e0/11
msgid ""
"Police, huh... Reminds me of the Costa Rican Civil\n"
"Guard.\n"
msgstr ""
"警察啊……想起哥斯达黎加\n"
"国民警卫队。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0330_000_0
#. timeline 13054..14349
#: codec/1/160/0xa04e0/12
msgid ""
"Yeah, exactly. They're also dispatched to provide\n"
"disaster relief.\n"
msgstr ""
"对，没错。他们也会被派去提供\n"
"灾害救援。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0330_000_0
#. timeline 14433..15130
#: codec/1/160/0xa04e0/13
msgid ""
"The year before I joined, they had a hell of a time\n"
msgstr ""
"我入伍前一年，他们可吃了不少苦头\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0330_000_0
#. timeline 15130..16063
#: codec/1/160/0xa04e0/14
msgid ""
"trying to rescue some buses that got hit by\n"
"landslides.\n"
msgstr ""
"去营救一些被\n"
"滑坡砸中的公交车。\n"

#: codec/1/160/0xa0a60/0
msgid ""
"So why'd you quit the JSDF?\n"
msgstr ""
"那你为什么退出日本自卫队？\n"

#: codec/1/160/0xa0a60/1
msgid ""
"Because I didn't have a reason to be in Japan\n"
"anymore.\n"
msgstr ""
"因为我已经没有理由\n"
"继续留在日本了。\n"

#: codec/1/160/0xa0a60/2
msgid ""
"Reason?\n"
msgstr ""
"理由？\n"

#: codec/1/160/0xa0a60/3
msgid ""
"My mom had died three years earlier, so I didn't\n"
"have to care for her anymore.\n"
msgstr ""
"我母亲三年前去世了，所以我不用\n"
"再照顾她了。\n"

#: codec/1/160/0xa0a60/4
msgid ""
"With her gone, there was no point hanging around\n"
"in Japan.\n"
msgstr ""
"她走了，待在日本\n"
"也没意义了。\n"

#: codec/1/160/0xa0a60/5
msgid ""
"Yeah, but a man with your talents could have risen\n"
"pretty high in the ranks, I imagine.\n"
msgstr ""
"是啊，但以你的才能，我想本可以在\n"
"军阶上爬得相当高。\n"

#: codec/1/160/0xa0a60/6
msgid ""
"I don't know what they made of me. Could be it\n"
"actually alienated me from the brass.\n"
msgstr ""
"我不知道他们怎么看我。可能这\n"
"反而让我和上级疏远了。\n"

#: codec/1/160/0xa0a60/7
msgid ""
"And personally, I could never get used to the idea\n"
"of exclusive defense.\n"
msgstr ""
"就我个人而言，始终无法接受\n"
"专守防卫这种理念。\n"

#: codec/1/160/0xa0a60/8
#: codec/2/905/0x389770/33
msgid ""
"Meaning?\n"
msgstr ""
"什么意思？\n"

#: codec/1/160/0xa0a60/9
msgid ""
"On a strategic level,\n"
msgstr ""
"战略上讲，\n"

#: codec/1/160/0xa0a60/10
msgid ""
"I can see how a country could go with the\n"
"exclusive defense model used by the JSDF,\n"
msgstr ""
"我能理解一个国家为什么会采用\n"
"自卫队那种专守防卫模式，\n"

#: codec/1/160/0xa0a60/11
msgid ""
"and I've got nothing against my fellow soldiers who\n"
"believe in it.\n"
msgstr ""
"而且我对信奉这一理念的\n"
"战友们没有任何意见。\n"

#: codec/1/160/0xa0a60/12
msgid ""
"On a tactical level, though, it just rubbed me the\n"
"wrong way.\n"
msgstr ""
"但战术层面，这实在让我\n"
"觉得不对劲。\n"

#: codec/1/160/0xa0a60/13
msgid ""
"To put it simply, I was itching for a real fight.\n"
msgstr ""
"简单说，我渴望真正的战斗。\n"

#: codec/1/160/0xa0a60/14
msgid ""
"I figured....\n"
msgstr ""
"我想……\n"

#: codec/1/160/0xa0a60/15
msgid ""
"And I felt like as long as I was in the JSDF,\n"
msgstr ""
"我觉得只要还在日本自卫队，\n"

#: codec/1/160/0xa0a60/16
msgid ""
"I'd never be able to stand shoulder to shoulder\n"
"with my father who was in the U.S. Army.\n"
msgstr ""
"我永远无法和我那曾在美军服役的\n"
"父亲并肩而立。\n"

#: codec/1/160/0xa0a60/17
msgid ""
"Seeing Yukio Mishima's suicide didn't help, either.\n"
msgstr ""
"三岛由纪夫的自杀也让我触动。\n"

#: codec/1/160/0xa0a60/18
msgid ""
"Yukio Mishima... the guy who wrote \"The Temple of\n"
"the Golden Pavilion\"?\n"
msgstr ""
"三岛由纪夫……就是写《金阁寺》的\n"
"那个人？\n"

#: codec/1/160/0xa0a60/19
msgid ""
"The way he questioned the status quo hit home\n"
"with me.\n"
msgstr ""
"他质疑现状的方式\n"
"让我深有共鸣。\n"

#: codec/1/160/0xa0a60/20
msgid ""
"Not that I admired his vision or anything. But it did\n"
"get me thinking, that's for sure.\n"
msgstr ""
"倒不是钦佩他的愿景。但这确实\n"
"让我思考很多，毫无疑问。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0020_000_0
#. timeline 445..1198
#: codec/1/161/0xa11f0/0
msgid ""
"Don't forget to give the MSF staff assignments.\n"
msgstr ""
"别忘了给MSF员工分配任务。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0020_000_0
#. timeline 1267..2173
#: codec/1/161/0xa11f0/1
msgid ""
"Where you place people will determine how Mother\n"
"Base grows..\n"
msgstr ""
"人员配置决定Mother\n"
"Base的发展。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0020_000_0
#. timeline 2396..3357
#: codec/1/161/0xa11f0/3
msgid ""
"That goes for me, too. Assign me wherever you\n"
"think is best.\n"
msgstr ""
"我也一样。把我派到\n"
"你觉得最合适的地方。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0020_000_0
#. timeline 3371..4193
#: codec/1/161/0xa11f0/4
msgid ""
"You? I thought you were second-in-command.\n"
msgstr ""
"你？你不是二把手吗。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0020_000_0
#. timeline 4207..4667
#: codec/1/161/0xa11f0/5
msgid ""
"Don't worry, I've got that covered.\n"
msgstr ""
"放心，那事我来管。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0020_000_0
#. timeline 4667..6018
#: codec/1/161/0xa11f0/6
msgid ""
"But MSF is still small, and I don't have the leisure\n"
"of sitting around on my butt all day.\n"
msgstr ""
"但MSF还小，我可没空\n"
"整天闲坐着。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0020_000_0
#. timeline 6673..7244
#: codec/1/161/0xa11f0/7
msgid ""
"I see your point, but...\n"
msgstr ""
"我懂，可是……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0020_000_0
#. timeline 7258..8442
#: codec/1/161/0xa11f0/8
msgid ""
"Not to brag or anything, but I'd kick ass at\n"
"whatever job you gave me.\n"
msgstr ""
"不是吹牛，你派我干啥\n"
"我都能干得漂亮。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0020_000_0
#. timeline 8456..9445
#: codec/1/161/0xa11f0/9
msgid ""
"Put me in the area you want to focus on\n"
"developing most.\n"
msgstr ""
"把我放到你最想重点\n"
"发展的领域。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0020_000_0
#. timeline 9473..10267
#: codec/1/161/0xa11f0/10
msgid ""
"I'll take real good care of the staff there.\n"
msgstr ""
"我会好好照顾那里的员工。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0020_000_0
#. timeline 10267..10699
#: codec/1/161/0xa11f0/11
msgid ""
"Easy, Kaz.\n"
msgstr ""
"别急，卡兹。\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/0
msgid ""
"March 10, 1945. 381,300 cluster bombs were\n"
"dropped on Tokyo.\n"
msgstr ""
"1945年3月10日，\n"
"东京遭到38万枚集束炸弹轰炸。\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/1
msgid ""
"Japanese houses at the time were almost all made\n"
"of wood.\n"
msgstr ""
"当时日本的房子\n"
"几乎都是木造的。\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/2
msgid ""
"In that single day, a third of Tokyo burned to the\n"
"ground.\n"
msgstr ""
"仅仅一天，东京就有三分之一\n"
"化为灰烬。\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/3
msgid ""
"My mom lost her family and home in that raid.\n"
msgstr ""
"我母亲在那次空袭中家破人亡。\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/4
msgid ""
"She had to move to Yokosuka and live with her\n"
"cousin.\n"
msgstr ""
"她只好搬到横须贺，\n"
"投靠亲戚。\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/5
msgid ""
"The B-29s kept on coming, razing other major\n"
"cities throughout Japan without mercy.\n"
msgstr ""
"B-29持续来袭，\n"
"毫不留情地把日本各地主要城市夷为平地。\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/6
msgid ""
"Then, in August, they dropped atomic bombs on\n"
"Hiroshima and Nagasaki,\n"
msgstr ""
"到了八月，\n"
"广岛和长崎又落下了原子弹，\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/7
msgid ""
"and Japan surrendered to the United States at last.\n"
msgstr ""
"日本终于向美国投降。\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/8
msgid ""
"After that, Yokosuka was flooded with American\n"
"soldiers come to occupy the country.\n"
msgstr ""
"此后，前来占领的美军士兵\n"
"涌满了横须贺。\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/9
msgid ""
"My mother was still in her mid-teens, and she\n"
"learned from her cousin\n"
msgstr ""
"母亲当时还不到二十岁，\n"
"她从亲戚那里学会了\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/10
msgid ""
"how to survive in that town - by servicing the\n"
"troops.\n"
msgstr ""
"如何在那镇上活下去：\n"
"靠招待大兵。\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/11
msgid ""
"That's how she met my father. And how I was born.\n"
msgstr ""
"她就是这样认识我父亲的，我也因此出生。\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/12
msgid ""
"My father was an officer\n"
msgstr ""
"我父亲是一名军官，\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/13
msgid ""
"serving with the Government Section of Allied GHQ,\n"
"under General Whitney.\n"
msgstr ""
"在盟军总司令部民政局服役，\n"
"隶属惠特尼将军麾下。\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/14
msgid ""
"Whitney was known as MacArthur's shadow,\n"
msgstr ""
"惠特尼人称麦克阿瑟的影子，\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/15
msgid ""
"and my father rode his coattails to a pretty high\n"
"rank.\n"
msgstr ""
"我父亲借着他的提携，\n"
"一路升到相当高的军衔。\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/16
msgid ""
"While he was in Japan, he treated my mom like a\n"
"wife.\n"
msgstr ""
"在日本期间，\n"
"他待我母亲如同妻子。\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/17
msgid ""
"After he went back to the States, though, she\n"
"never heard from him.\n"
msgstr ""
"可他一回到美国，\n"
"就再没有音信。\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/18
msgid ""
"I wasn't born until after he went back.\n"
msgstr ""
"他走之后我才出生。\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/19
msgid ""
"My mom raised me as a single mother.\n"
msgstr ""
"母亲一个人把我拉扯大。\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/20
msgid ""
"She used the money my father left her to open a\n"
"shop,\n"
msgstr ""
"她用我父亲留下的钱\n"
"开了家店，\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/21
msgid ""
"selling cigarettes and stuff to occupation troops.\n"
msgstr ""
"卖香烟之类的东西给占领军。\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/22
msgid ""
"It was a decent living. But I didn't have citizenship.\n"
msgstr ""
"日子还过得去。但我没有国籍。\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/23
msgid ""
"They're working to change the law now, but back\n"
"then, if your father was unknown,\n"
msgstr ""
"现在他们在推动修法，\n"
"可在当时，如果生父不明，\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/24
msgid ""
"you couldn't get onto the Japanese family register\n"
msgstr ""
"就上不了日本的户籍，\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/25
msgid ""
"- and in Japan, that means you can't be Japanese.\n"
msgstr ""
"——在日本，这就意味着你不是日本人。\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/26
msgid ""
"So as I watched the American soldiers around\n"
"town, I said to myself:\n"
msgstr ""
"看着镇上四处走动的美军士兵，\n"
"我对自己说：\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/27
msgid ""
"I'm a son of America, the victor.\n"
msgstr ""
"我是战胜国美国的儿子。\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/28
msgid ""
"My hair and eyes were different from the skinny,\n"
"downtrodden Japanese around me.\n"
msgstr ""
"我的头发和眼睛，都和周围那些\n"
"瘦弱憔悴的日本人不同。\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/29
msgid ""
"I told myself I'd leave this country someday and\n"
"return to my true homeland..\n"
msgstr ""
"我告诉自己，总有一天要离开这里，\n"
"回到真正的祖国……\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/30
msgid ""
"When I was around 10 years old, my mom fell ill,\n"
msgstr ""
"我十岁左右时，母亲病倒了，\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/31
msgid ""
"pretty much leaving me to run the shop in her\n"
"place.\n"
msgstr ""
"店里的事基本\n"
"就落到了我身上。\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/32
msgid ""
"One day, I found a single picture of my father in\n"
"the back of a drawer in the shop.\n"
msgstr ""
"有一天，我在店铺抽屉深处\n"
"发现了父亲的一张照片。\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/33
msgid ""
"I'd show it to the American soldiers who came in to\n"
"the store.\n"
msgstr ""
"我把它拿给\n"
"来店里的大兵们看。\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/34
msgid ""
"A few years went by before one of them told me\n"
"who he was.\n"
msgstr ""
"过了几年，才有个人\n"
"告诉我他是谁。\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/35
msgid ""
"\"I know him. That's Miller.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"「我认识他。那是米勒。」\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/36
msgid ""
"I started asking other guys. \"Do you know where\n"
"Miller is now?\"\n"
msgstr ""
"我开始向别人打听。“你们知道\n"
"米勒现在在哪吗？”\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/37
msgid ""
"\"Can anybody tell me where Colonel Miller is now?\"\n"
msgstr ""
"“有谁能告诉我米勒上校现在在哪？”\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/38
msgid ""
"Turns out he'd left the service\n"
msgstr ""
"原来他早已退伍\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/39
msgid ""
"and was making a living as an instructor for\n"
"soldiers in Virginia.\n"
msgstr ""
"在弗吉尼亚靠当教官\n"
"训兵为生。\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/40
msgid ""
"It was one of his students who finally told me that.\n"
msgstr ""
"是他的一个学生最终告诉我的。\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/41
msgid ""
"I wrote him a letter in English. \"I'm your son. I want\n"
"to go to the United States.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"我用英文写了封信。“我是\n"
"您儿子。我想去美国。”\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/42
msgid ""
"Day after day, I waited. Then, just when I was\n"
"about to give up,\n"
msgstr ""
"一天天过去，我等着。\n"
"就在我快要放弃时，\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/43
msgid ""
"the post office delivered my future to the door.\n"
msgstr ""
"邮局把我的未来送到了门口。\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/44
msgid ""
"My father sent me some money. I thought my\n"
"dream was going to come true.\n"
msgstr ""
"父亲寄来了钱。我以为\n"
"梦想就要实现了。\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/45
msgid ""
"I was only thinking of myself.\n"
msgstr ""
"我心里只想着自己。\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/46
msgid ""
"So I went to my bedridden mother and convinced\n"
"her to let me go.\n"
msgstr ""
"于是我去找卧床的母亲，\n"
"说服她让我走。\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/47
msgid ""
"My father arranged for a car to pick me up. It was\n"
"jet-black.\n"
msgstr ""
"父亲安排了车来接我。\n"
"那车漆黑发亮。\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/48
msgid ""
"When the neighborhood kids who'd always made\n"
"fun of my hair saw it,\n"
msgstr ""
"邻居家那些总嘲笑我\n"
"头发的孩子看见那车，\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/49
msgid ""
"their jaws practically hit the ground.\n"
msgstr ""
"下巴差点掉到地上。\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/50
msgid ""
"I put my mom in a hospital, and went on my own to\n"
"America.\n"
msgstr ""
"我把母亲送进医院，\n"
"独自去了美国。\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/51
msgid ""
"When I met my father for the first time, he was\n"
"living alone in a big house.\n"
msgstr ""
"第一次见到父亲时，他\n"
"独居在一栋大房子里。\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/52
msgid ""
"He told me he'd lost his son... his American son... in\n"
"Vietnam.\n"
msgstr ""
"他说他在越南失去了儿子……\n"
"他那个美国儿子……\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/53
msgid ""
"He showed me a picture. A picture of my older\n"
"brother.\n"
msgstr ""
"他给我看了一张照片。\n"
"我哥哥的照片。\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/54
msgid ""
"I guess that and his divorce left my father feeling\n"
"lonely...\n"
msgstr ""
"我想，那件事加上离婚，\n"
"让父亲感到孤独……\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/55
msgid ""
"which is probably why he finally took an interest in\n"
"me.\n"
msgstr ""
"大概所以他终于\n"
"对我有了兴趣。\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/56
msgid ""
"He'd retired from teaching. He was stooped over,\n"
"could hardly walk.\n"
msgstr ""
"他已经从教官职位上退下来，\n"
"驼着背，几乎走不动路。\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/57
msgid ""
"But he gave me two things: the name Miller, and\n"
"money for school.\n"
msgstr ""
"但他给了我两样东西：\n"
"米勒这个姓，和上学的钱。\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/58
msgid ""
"I used it to learn English and then go to college.\n"
msgstr ""
"我用它学英文，然后上了大学。\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/59
msgid ""
"America was exhausted from years of fighting in\n"
"Vietnam.\n"
msgstr ""
"美国因长年在越南作战\n"
"而疲惫不堪。\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/60
msgid ""
"They were waging war in a foreign land while at\n"
"home people were screaming for peace.\n"
msgstr ""
"他们在异国打仗，国内\n"
"民众却在疾呼和平。\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/61
msgid ""
"Right after I graduated, I went back to Japan.\n"
"Alone.\n"
msgstr ""
"一毕业，我就回了日本。\n"
"一个人。\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/62
msgid ""
"My father refused to see my mom.\n"
msgstr ""
"父亲不肯见母亲。\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/63
msgid ""
"It was the first time I'd seen her in years, and she\n"
"wouldn't even look at me.\n"
msgstr ""
"那是多年后我第一次见她，\n"
"她却连看都不看我。\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/64
msgid ""
"At first I thought she was mad at me.\n"
msgstr ""
"起初我以为她在生我的气。\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/65
msgid ""
"But that wasn't it. Disease had taken her mind...\n"
msgstr ""
"但不是。病魔夺走了她的神智……\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/66
msgid ""
"A disease she'd gotten when she was young and\n"
"desperate.\n"
msgstr ""
"那是她年轻、走投无路时\n"
"染上的病。\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/67
msgid ""
"She didn't even know who I was.\n"
msgstr ""
"她连我是谁都不知道了。\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/68
msgid ""
"I said, \"Mom, it's me, Kazuhira.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"我说：“妈，是我，和平。”\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/69
msgid ""
"As I spoke, the sound of my own voice rang in my\n"
"ears.\n"
msgstr ""
"说着，我自己的声音\n"
"在耳边回响。\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/70
msgid ""
"Kazuhira. The name my mom gave me. It means\n"
"\"peace\" in Japanese.\n"
msgstr ""
"和平。母亲给我取的名字。\n"
"在日语里是“和平”之意。\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/71
msgid ""
"I was Japanese. At least, I was the son of this tiny\n"
"Japanese woman.\n"
msgstr ""
"我是日本人。至少，我是\n"
"这个瘦小日本女人的儿子。\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/72
msgid ""
"It was then, for the first time, that I understood\n"
"the reason\n"
msgstr ""
"就在那时，我第一次\n"
"明白了缘由——\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/73
msgid ""
"- the emotion - that inspired my mother to give me\n"
"that name.\n"
msgstr ""
"——那份让母亲给我\n"
"取这个名字的情感。\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/74
msgid ""
"She'd watched her hometown and family go up in\n"
"flames.\n"
msgstr ""
"她目睹故乡与家人\n"
"葬身火海。\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/75
msgid ""
"Her body and her mind were ravaged by war...\n"
msgstr ""
"她的身心都被战争摧残……\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/76
msgid ""
"And yet she chose to have a child named \"peace,\"\n"
msgstr ""
"可她仍生下了一个叫“和平”的孩子，\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/77
msgid ""
"with a man who was once her enemy.\n"
msgstr ""
"和一个曾是敌人的人生下的。\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/78
msgid ""
"Japan lost the war. But what good is war as a\n"
"measure of a country?\n"
msgstr ""
"日本输了战争。可战争\n"
"又怎能衡量一个国家？\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/79
msgid ""
"Since the war, and up until the oil shock last year,\n"
msgstr ""
"战后直到去年的石油危机，\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/80
msgid ""
"Japan's economy has grown every single year.\n"
msgstr ""
"日本经济年年都在增长。\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/81
msgid ""
"It's on its way to becoming a stronger country\n"
"than ever.\n"
msgstr ""
"它正变得比以往\n"
"任何时候都强大。\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/82
msgid ""
"I stayed in Japan and joined the JSDF. I was\n"
"twenty-two at the time.\n"
msgstr ""
"我留在日本加入了自卫队。\n"
"那年我二十二岁。\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/83
msgid ""
"I did it to pay our bills... but it wasn't just that. I\n"
"could have found work anywhere.\n"
msgstr ""
"我是为了付账单……但也不全是。\n"
"在哪都能找到工作。\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/84
msgid ""
"And I knew it. And still, I couldn't think of anything\n"
"else to do with myself.\n"
msgstr ""
"我明白这一点。可除此之外，\n"
"我想不出还能做什么。\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/85
msgid ""
"Two years later, I didn't have to worry about mom's\n"
"hospital bills anymore...\n"
msgstr ""
"两年后，母亲的住院费\n"
"再也不用我操心了……\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/86
msgid ""
"I left the JSDF and went back to the States.\n"
msgstr ""
"我离开自卫队，回到了美国。\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/87
msgid ""
"My father was already dead and buried. I was told\n"
"he'd shot himself in the head.\n"
msgstr ""
"父亲早已下葬。他们告诉我，\n"
"他是对着自己的头开的枪。\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/88
msgid ""
"America crushed Japan. But it also crushed my\n"
"father.\n"
msgstr ""
"美国击垮了日本。\n"
"也击垮了我的父亲。\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/89
msgid ""
"My American Dream was over.\n"
msgstr ""
"我的美国梦结束了。\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/90
msgid ""
"After that, I drifted around and... well, you know the\n"
"rest.\n"
msgstr ""
"之后我四处漂泊……\n"
"后来的事你都知道了。\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/91
msgid ""
"...GHQ made women like my mother.\n"
msgstr ""
"……是盟军总司令部造就了母亲那样的女人。\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/92
msgid ""
"It made Japan's peace constitution and the JSDF.\n"
"And it made me.\n"
msgstr ""
"它造就了日本的和平宪法\n"
"与自卫队。也造就了我。\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/93
msgid ""
"I was spawned by war. But I don't want to die in\n"
"one.\n"
msgstr ""
"我生于战争。\n"
"但我不想死于战争。\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/94
msgid ""
"I won't die for a country, and I won't live like a\n"
"pauper.\n"
msgstr ""
"我不会为国家而死，\n"
"也不会像乞丐一样活着。\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/95
msgid ""
"I won't have my fate decided by some family\n"
"register.\n"
msgstr ""
"我不会让一本户籍\n"
"决定我的命运。\n"

#: codec/1/161/0xa15f0/96
msgid ""
"So as long as I stick with you, Boss, I've got a\n"
"good feeling none of that will happen.\n"
msgstr ""
"所以只要跟着你，BOSS，\n"
"我预感这些都不会发生。\n"

#: codec/1/163/0xa3900/0
msgid ""
"Life's funny sometimes, isn't it?\n"
msgstr ""
"人生有时真奇妙，不是吗？\n"

#: codec/1/163/0xa3900/1
msgid ""
"What brought that on?\n"
msgstr ""
"怎么突然说起这个？\n"

#: codec/1/163/0xa3900/2
msgid ""
"We first met as enemies on the battlefield, and\n"
"now here we are fighting side by side.\n"
msgstr ""
"我们最初是在战场上相遇的敌人，\n"
"如今却并肩作战。\n"

#: codec/1/163/0xa3900/3
msgid ""
"You mean Colombia?\n"
msgstr ""
"你是说哥伦比亚？\n"

#: codec/1/163/0xa3900/4
msgid ""
"Yeah. After I quit the JSDF, I made my way there\n"
"and got myself a position\n"
msgstr ""
"对。我退出自卫队后就去了那里，\n"
"谋了个职位——\n"

#: codec/1/163/0xa3900/5
msgid ""
"as a drill sergeant for a band of revolutionaries,\n"
msgstr ""
"给一帮革命军当教官，\n"

#: codec/1/163/0xa3900/6
msgid ""
"despite the fact that I'd never seen a day of\n"
"combat.\n"
msgstr ""
"尽管我一天\n"
"实战经验都没有。\n"

#: codec/1/163/0xa3900/7
msgid ""
"I see you had the gift for talking business in\n"
"Spanish even back then.\n"
msgstr ""
"看来你那时就很有\n"
"用西班牙语谈生意的天赋。\n"

#: codec/1/163/0xa3900/8
msgid ""
"C'mon, stop it, you're making me blush.\n"
msgstr ""
"行了行了，别说得我不好意思。\n"

#: codec/1/163/0xa3900/9
msgid ""
"Unlucky for me, though, you were in the service of\n"
"the Colombian Army.\n"
msgstr ""
"可我不走运，你当时\n"
"效力于哥伦比亚政府军。\n"

#: codec/1/163/0xa3900/10
msgid ""
"I remember it like it was yesterday. It all happened\n"
"in an instant.\n"
msgstr ""
"那件事我记忆犹新，\n"
"一切都发生在一瞬间。\n"

#: codec/1/163/0xa3900/11
msgid ""
"You guys ambushed us, and half my unit was taken\n"
"out.\n"
msgstr ""
"你们伏击了我们，\n"
"我半个分队都被打掉了。\n"

#: codec/1/163/0xa3900/12
msgid ""
"My mind went totally blank. I couldn't keep it\n"
"together... My whole unit was wiped out...\n"
msgstr ""
"我脑子里一片空白，完全慌了神……\n"
"整个分队都被歼灭了……\n"

#: codec/1/163/0xa3900/13
msgid ""
"and I was left half-dead from a bomb blast.\n"
msgstr ""
"我也被炸得半死。\n"

#: codec/1/163/0xa3900/14
msgid ""
"Then, as I was leaving, you yelled out at me...\n"
msgstr ""
"就在我准备撤退时，你冲我喊道……\n"

#: codec/1/163/0xa3900/15
msgid ""
"\"I came all the way from Japan to be here. My\n"
"place is on the battlefield.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"「我从日本远道而来，\n"
"我的归宿就是战场。」\n"

#: codec/1/163/0xa3900/16
msgid ""
"Then you asked for my help, saying, \"I want to be\n"
"the one to end it.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"然后你向我求助，说：\n"
"「我要亲手结束这一切。」\n"

#: codec/1/163/0xa3900/17
msgid ""
"I remember being surprised that there were still\n"
"samurai in Japan.\n"
msgstr ""
"我记得当时很惊讶：\n"
"日本竟然还有武士。\n"

#: codec/1/163/0xa3900/18
msgid ""
"You guys came over to me. I had a grenade hidden\n"
"under me.\n"
msgstr ""
"你们向我走来。\n"
"我身下藏着一枚手榴弹。\n"

#: codec/1/163/0xa3900/19
msgid ""
"But even then you were too fast. The second I\n"
"pulled the pin,\n"
msgstr ""
"可即便如此，你还是太快了。\n"
"我刚拉掉保险销，\n"

#: codec/1/163/0xa3900/20
msgid ""
"you grabbed the hand I was using to hold the\n"
"grenade with both palms.\n"
msgstr ""
"你就用双手\n"
"抓住了我握弹的那只手。\n"

#: codec/1/163/0xa3900/21
msgid ""
"I didn't want it to go off. I'd heard samurai were a\n"
"proud bunch. I wanted to know\n"
msgstr ""
"我不想让它爆炸。听说武士很骄傲，\n"
"我想知道\n"

#: codec/1/163/0xa3900/22
msgid ""
"why one of them would stoop so low as to try and\n"
"take his opponent with him.\n"
msgstr ""
"为什么有人会卑劣到\n"
"想把对手一起拖下水。\n"

#: codec/1/163/0xa3900/23
msgid ""
"And I said, \"I'll never lose again... We'll never lose\n"
"again.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"于是我说：「我再也不会输了……\n"
"我们再也不会输。」\n"

#: codec/1/163/0xa3900/24
msgid ""
"Yeah. \"We'll do whatever it takes, but we'll never be\n"
"beaten again.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"对。「我们不惜一切，\n"
"也绝不再败。」\n"

#: codec/1/163/0xa3900/25
msgid ""
"Then I passed out from the blood loss.\n"
msgstr ""
"然后我就因失血昏迷了。\n"

#: codec/1/163/0xa3900/26
msgid ""
"When I woke up, I was in your camp's infirmary,\n"
"stuck full of tubes.\n"
msgstr ""
"醒来时，我躺在你们营地\n"
"的医务室，浑身插满管子。\n"

#: codec/1/163/0xa3900/27
msgid ""
"Why'd you save me, your enemy, after I tried to kill\n"
"you?\n"
msgstr ""
"我可是想杀你的敌人，\n"
"你为什么救我？\n"

#: codec/1/163/0xa3900/28
msgid ""
"Because you swallowed your pride and fought with\n"
"everything you had.\n"
msgstr ""
"因为你放下尊严，\n"
"拼尽了一切去战斗。\n"

#: codec/1/163/0xa3900/29
msgid ""
"I just didn't want to lose...\n"
msgstr ""
"我只是不想输……\n"

#: codec/1/163/0xa3900/30
msgid ""
"You found a way to fight back even in the face of\n"
"death\n"
msgstr ""
"即便面对死亡，你仍\n"
"找到了反击的办法\n"

#: codec/1/163/0xa3900/31
msgid ""
"- even when you knew you were going to die.\n"
"That's the mark of a true warrior.\n"
msgstr ""
"——明知会死也依然如此。\n"
"那是真正战士的资质。\n"

#: codec/1/163/0xa3900/32
msgid ""
"It's not about gain and loss, or victory and defeat.\n"
msgstr ""
"这与得失、胜负无关。\n"

#: codec/1/163/0xa3900/33
msgid ""
"I looked at the way you lived your life and saw the\n"
"path I needed to take. As a warrior.\n"
msgstr ""
"看着你的活法，我看见了\n"
"自己该走的路。作为战士的路。\n"

#: codec/1/163/0xa3900/34
msgid ""
"Wow. I never knew that. And that's why you...\n"
msgstr ""
"哇。我从不知道。所以你才……\n"

#: codec/1/163/0xa3900/35
msgid ""
"I realized then that the battlefield doesn't only\n"
"divide people into allies and enemies.\n"
msgstr ""
"那时我明白，战场不只把人\n"
"分成友军和敌人。\n"

#: codec/1/163/0xa3900/36
msgid ""
"Sometimes it tells you more than just who's an ally\n"
"or who's an enemy.\n"
msgstr ""
"它有时还会告诉你\n"
"比敌友更多的东西。\n"

#: codec/1/163/0xa3900/37
msgid ""
"Sometimes it helps reveal your true comrades.\n"
msgstr ""
"有时它能让你看清真正的同志。\n"

#: codec/1/163/0xa3900/38
msgid ""
"Like you and me, huh?\n"
msgstr ""
"比如你和我，是吧？\n"

#: codec/1/163/0xa3900/39
msgid ""
"That's right. And two years later, here we are...\n"
msgstr ""
"没错。两年后的今天，我们就在这里……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0010_000_0
#. timeline 445..1156
#: codec/1/164/0xa47a0/0
msgid ""
"You've probably heard this a million times, Snake,\n"
msgstr ""
"这话你可能听过无数遍了，SNAKE，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0010_000_0
#. timeline 1170..2117
#: codec/1/164/0xa47a0/1
msgid ""
"but you should always avoid combat with the\n"
"enemy when possible.\n"
msgstr ""
"但只要能避免，就尽量别和\n"
"敌人交战。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0010_000_0
#. timeline 2382..3218
#: codec/1/164/0xa47a0/3
msgid ""
"We're outnumbered and in unfamiliar territory.\n"
msgstr ""
"我们人少，又在陌生地带。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0010_000_0
#. timeline 3232..4416
#: codec/1/164/0xa47a0/4
msgid ""
"We won't survive long in a straight fight, even with\n"
"you on our side.\n"
msgstr ""
"正面硬拼撑不了多久，就算\n"
"有你在也一样。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0010_000_0
#. timeline 4444..5781
#: codec/1/164/0xa47a0/5
msgid ""
"I know. Avoiding combat is rule number one in a\n"
"sneaking mission.\n"
msgstr ""
"我知道。潜入任务第一条\n"
"就是避免交战。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0010_000_0
#. timeline 5795..7174
#: codec/1/164/0xa47a0/6
msgid ""
"That's right. Don't let the enemy know where you\n"
"are, and attack only when necessary,\n"
msgstr ""
"没错。别让敌人发现你的\n"
"位置，只在必要时出手，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0010_000_0
#. timeline 7174..7955
#: codec/1/164/0xa47a0/7
msgid ""
"using hit-and-run tactics to cripple them...\n"
msgstr ""
"用打了就跑的战术削弱他们……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0010_000_0
#. timeline 8010..8693
#: codec/1/164/0xa47a0/8
msgid ""
"It's the essence of guerrilla warfare.\n"
msgstr ""
"这就是游击战的精髓。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0650_000_0
#. timeline 459..919
#: codec/1/164/0xa4b00/0
msgid ""
"Can I ask you a favor, Snake?\n"
msgstr ""
"能拜托你件事吗，SNAKE？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0650_000_0
#. timeline 919..1657
#: codec/1/164/0xa4b00/1
msgid ""
"If you ask nicely.\n"
msgstr ""
"你好好求我就行。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0650_000_0
#. timeline 1657..2605
#: codec/1/164/0xa4b00/2
msgid ""
"To make MSF bigger, we need to do some\n"
"recruiting.\n"
msgstr ""
"要壮大MSF，就得\n"
"招些人手。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0650_000_0
#. timeline 2605..3371
#: codec/1/164/0xa4b00/3
msgid ""
"Yeah... What's your point?\n"
msgstr ""
"嗯……你想说啥？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0650_000_0
#. timeline 3371..5224
#: codec/1/164/0xa4b00/4
msgid ""
"I want you to avoid killing enemy soldiers as much\n"
"as possible and send them back using Fulton\n"
"recovery.\n"
msgstr ""
"我希望你尽量避免杀死敌方士兵\n"
"尽可能用富尔顿回收\n"
"把他们送回来。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0650_000_0
#. timeline 5224..6032
#: codec/1/164/0xa4b00/5
msgid ""
"Not much we can do with a corpse except give it a\n"
"funeral.\n"
msgstr ""
"尸体除了下葬\n"
"也没别的用。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0650_000_0
#. timeline 6032..6352
#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_myo_rad_0120_000_0
#. timeline 4750..5140
#: codec/1/164/0xa4b00/6
#: codec/2/917/0x395bd0/6
msgid ""
"Obviously.\n"
msgstr ""
"当然。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0650_000_0
#. timeline 6366..7272
#: codec/1/164/0xa4b00/7
msgid ""
"Put 'em to sleep, knock 'em out...hold 'em up, even.\n"
msgstr ""
"打晕、弄睡……甚至逼降都行。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0650_000_0
#. timeline 7272..8526
#: codec/1/164/0xa4b00/8
msgid ""
"And if you do have to fight, try to leave them near\n"
"death instead of dead.\n"
msgstr ""
"真要打，尽量让他们濒死\n"
"而不是死亡。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0650_000_0
#. timeline 8540..9849
#: codec/1/164/0xa4b00/9
msgid ""
"And then use the Fulton recovery system...sounds\n"
"easy enough.\n"
msgstr ""
"然后用富尔顿回收系统……听着\n"
"挺简单。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0650_000_0
#. timeline 9863..11772
#: codec/1/164/0xa4b00/10
msgid ""
"You know what'd be really nice, though. If we had a\n"
"way to Fulton recover anybody at anytime...\n"
msgstr ""
"不过要是能随时\n"
"富尔顿回收任何人就好了……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0690_000_0
#. timeline 445..1337
#: codec/1/164/0xa4f10/0
msgid ""
"You can steal items from soldiers by putting them\n"
"to sleep\n"
msgstr ""
"让士兵睡着\n"
"就能偷走他们的物品，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0690_000_0
#. timeline 1337..2159
#: codec/1/164/0xa4f10/1
msgid ""
"or knocking them out and then doing a body check.\n"
msgstr ""
"或者打晕他们再搜身。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0690_000_0
#. timeline 2187..2814
#: codec/1/164/0xa4f10/2
msgid ""
"Get close to the unconscious soldier\n"
msgstr ""
"靠近失去意识的士兵，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0690_000_0
#. timeline 2814..3691
#: codec/1/164/0xa4f10/3
msgid ""
"and press <I=ACT> when you see the icon.\n"
msgstr ""
"看到图标时按<I=ACT>。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0690_000_0
#. timeline 3747..4820
#: codec/1/164/0xa4f10/4
msgid ""
"Or you can sneak up on them from behind and do\n"
"a hold-up.\n"
msgstr ""
"或者从背后悄悄靠近，\n"
"来一次挟持。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0690_000_0
#. timeline 4834..5586
#: codec/1/164/0xa4f10/5
msgid ""
"It also works if the soldier's near death.\n"
msgstr ""
"士兵濒死时同样有效。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0690_000_0
#. timeline 5600..6269
#: codec/1/164/0xa4f10/6
msgid ""
"Keep in mind, though - if you wait too long,\n"
msgstr ""
"不过要记住——拖得太久，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0690_000_0
#. timeline 6269..7091
#: codec/1/164/0xa4f10/7
msgid ""
"you'll have a dead soldier instead of a dying one.\n"
msgstr ""
"到你手里的就是死人而不是伤兵了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0690_000_0
#. timeline 7105..8359
#: codec/1/164/0xa4f10/8
msgid ""
"And you can't do a body check if you're holding\n"
"the Fulton recovery device, either.\n"
msgstr ""
"而且手里拿着富尔顿回收装置时，\n"
"也没法做身体检查。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0690_000_0
#. timeline 8387..8818
#: codec/1/164/0xa4f10/9
msgid ""
"So don't try.\n"
msgstr ""
"所以别白费劲。\n"

#: codec/1/165/0xa5290/0
msgid ""
"Don't carry any more gear than you need.\n"
msgstr ""
"别带多余的装备。\n"

#: codec/1/165/0xa5290/1
msgid ""
"If you try and stuff your entire arsenal into your\n"
"backpack,\n"
msgstr ""
"如果你试图把你的全部武器都塞进\n"
"背包里，\n"

#: codec/1/165/0xa5290/2
msgid ""
"it'll be too heavy and your mobility will be impaired.\n"
msgstr ""
"太重会拖慢你的行动。\n"

#: codec/1/165/0xa5290/3
msgid ""
"You'll only be hurting yourself.\n"
msgstr ""
"吃亏的是你自己。\n"

#: codec/1/165/0xa5290/4
msgid ""
"I know. Take only what you need. Every rookie\n"
"knows that.\n"
msgstr ""
"我知道。只带需要的。新兵\n"
"都懂。\n"

#: codec/1/165/0xa5290/5
msgid ""
"You can check the weight of your gear before\n"
"heading out.\n"
msgstr ""
"你可以在出发前检查\n"
"装备的重量。\n"

#: codec/1/165/0xa5290/6
msgid ""
"So make sure you do.\n"
msgstr ""
"记得查一下。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0050_000_0
#. timeline 445..1476
#: codec/1/165/0xa5540/0
msgid ""
"Even a born warrior like you gets hand tremors,\n"
"Snake.\n"
msgstr ""
"就算你这种天生战士也会手抖，\n"
"Snake。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0050_000_0
#. timeline 1518..2229
#: codec/1/165/0xa5540/1
msgid ""
"It happens even when you're full of stamina,\n"
msgstr ""
"体力满时也会抖，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0050_000_0
#. timeline 2229..3747
#: codec/1/165/0xa5540/2
msgid ""
"and it only gets worse when you're tired -\n"
"especially with larger, heavier weapons.\n"
msgstr ""
"累了只会更糟，\n"
"尤其拿更大更重的武器时。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0050_000_0
#. timeline 3775..4890
#: codec/1/165/0xa5540/3
msgid ""
"Obviously, you'll get better aim crouching than you\n"
"will standing.\n"
msgstr ""
"显然，蹲下时你的瞄准会比\n"
"站立时更好。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0050_000_0
#. timeline 4904..5976
#: codec/1/165/0xa5540/4
msgid ""
"And when you use a scope, setting your sights on\n"
"a single point\n"
msgstr ""
"而当你使用瞄准镜时，将准星对准\n"
"一个点\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0050_000_0
#. timeline 5976..6840
#: codec/1/165/0xa5540/5
msgid ""
"will gradually give you a more precise aim.\n"
msgstr ""
"瞄准会逐渐更精准。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0050_000_0
#. timeline 6924..7732
#: codec/1/165/0xa5540/6
msgid ""
"As we develop better weapons at Mother Base,\n"
"though,\n"
msgstr ""
"母基地造出好武器后，\n"
"不过，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0050_000_0
#. timeline 7732..8986
#: codec/1/165/0xa5540/7
msgid ""
"you may gain access to new, low-tremor versions\n"
"of the same guns.\n"
msgstr ""
"你可能会获得同一批枪械的新的、低抖动\n"
"版本。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0050_000_0
#. timeline 9000..9710
#: codec/1/165/0xa5540/8
msgid ""
"So if you expect the shakes to be a problem,\n"
msgstr ""
"要是担心手抖，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0050_000_0
#. timeline 9752..10574
#: codec/1/165/0xa5540/9
msgid ""
"you might want to put some resources into R&D.\n"
msgstr ""
"不妨投点资源搞研发。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0050_000_0
#. timeline 10574..11744
#: codec/1/165/0xa5540/10
msgid ""
"I'll keep it in mind. Then again, the more you use a\n"
"weapon,\n"
msgstr ""
"记下了。话说你越用一件\n"
"武器，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0050_000_0
#. timeline 11744..12301
#: codec/1/165/0xa5540/11
msgid ""
"the more your hands get used to it.\n"
msgstr ""
"手就越习惯。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0050_000_0
#. timeline 12301..13193
#: codec/1/165/0xa5540/12
msgid ""
"Sometimes it pays to be faithful to your gun.\n"
msgstr ""
"忠于自己的枪有时也有好处。\n"

#: codec/1/165/0xa5a00/0
msgid ""
"Choosing the right uniform is crucial.\n"
msgstr ""
"选对制服很关键。\n"

#: codec/1/165/0xa5a00/1
msgid ""
"Pick one that matches the mission objective and\n"
"your own combat style.\n"
msgstr ""
"挑一个既符合任务目标、\n"
"又契合你战斗风格的吧。\n"

#: codec/1/165/0xa5b10/0
msgid ""
"Jungle fatigues are made for jungle combat.\n"
msgstr ""
"丛林迷彩就是为丛林战设计的。\n"

#: codec/1/165/0xa5b10/1
msgid ""
"They provide decent protection and let you carry\n"
"a fair number of weapons. Your standard uniform,\n"
"basically.\n"
msgstr ""
"防护不错，还能带\n"
"不少武器。基本就是你的\n"
"标准制服。\n"

#: codec/1/165/0xa5b10/2
msgid ""
"The distinguishing factor is that your camo index\n"
"will vary - a lot - depending on the area.\n"
msgstr ""
"区别在于，你的迷彩指数\n"
"会因区域不同而大幅变化。\n"

#: codec/1/165/0xa5b10/3
msgid ""
"Wear a pattern that makes you blend in with your\n"
"surroundings and your camo index goes up.\n"
msgstr ""
"穿上能让你融入周围环境的\n"
"迷彩，你的迷彩指数就会上升。\n"

#: codec/1/165/0xa5b10/4
msgid ""
"Wear something that clashes and you'll stick out\n"
"like a sore thumb.\n"
msgstr ""
"穿得格格不入，你就会\n"
"特别显眼。\n"

#: codec/1/165/0xa5b10/5
msgid ""
"Pick the right pattern for the occasion - Sigint\n"
"used to lecture me on it all the time.\n"
msgstr ""
"根据场合选对迷彩——Sigint\n"
"以前老是跟我念叨这个。\n"

#: codec/1/165/0xa5e20/0
msgid ""
"The sneaking suit is a specialized uniform for\n"
"stealth missions.\n"
msgstr ""
"潜行服是专为\n"
"潜行任务设计的特殊制服。\n"

#: codec/1/165/0xa5e20/1
msgid ""
"It provides excellent camo in any stage.\n"
msgstr ""
"任何地形都能提供极佳迷彩。\n"

#: codec/1/165/0xa5e20/2
msgid ""
"Even better, you won't make a sound when you\n"
"walk.\n"
msgstr ""
"更妙的是，走路时\n"
"不会出声。\n"

#: codec/1/165/0xa5e20/3
msgid ""
"So I won't need to tiptoe all the time.\n"
msgstr ""
"那我就不用一直踮着脚了。\n"

#: codec/1/165/0xa5e20/4
msgid ""
"And, to top it off, it also makes your wounds heal\n"
"faster.\n"
msgstr ""
"而且它还能让伤口\n"
"好得更快。\n"

#: codec/1/165/0xa5e20/5
msgid ""
"The fabric exerts just the right amount of\n"
"pressure on your body to help stop bleeding.\n"
msgstr ""
"这种面料会对你的身体施加恰到好处的\n"
"压力，帮助止血。\n"

#: codec/1/165/0xa5e20/6
msgid ""
"Not a bad little trick.\n"
msgstr ""
"这招不错。\n"

#: codec/1/166/0xa60d0/0
msgid ""
"The battle dress uniform is the opposite of the\n"
"sneaking suit\n"
msgstr ""
"战斗服与潜行服\n"
"正好相反\n"

#: codec/1/166/0xa60d0/1
msgid ""
"in that it's specialized for combat.\n"
msgstr ""
"它是专为战斗设计的。\n"

#: codec/1/166/0xa60d0/2
msgid ""
"It lets you carry plenty of weapons and ammo, and\n"
"provides excellent protection.\n"
msgstr ""
"它能让你携带大量武器和弹药，并\n"
"提供出色的防护。\n"

#: codec/1/166/0xa60d0/3
msgid ""
"Not the best choice for sneaking, but if you feel\n"
"like playing one-man army,\n"
msgstr ""
"虽然不适合潜行，但如果你想\n"
"玩一人成军的话，\n"

#: codec/1/166/0xa60d0/4
msgid ""
"this is the uniform of choice.\n"
msgstr ""
"就选它。\n"

#: codec/1/166/0xa60d0/5
msgid ""
"Looks pretty damn heavy.\n"
msgstr ""
"看着真够沉的。\n"

#: codec/1/166/0xa60d0/6
msgid ""
"It is. You won't be able to move as fast with it on,\n"
msgstr ""
"确实。穿上它移动会变慢，\n"

#: codec/1/166/0xa60d0/7
msgid ""
"meaning it's not good for running away, either.\n"
"Keep that in mind.\n"
msgstr ""
"也就是说它也不适合逃跑。\n"
"记住这一点。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0040_040_0
#. timeline 459..1462
#: codec/1/166/0xa63e0/0
msgid ""
"Naked... That's exactly what you are with this\n"
"uniform.\n"
msgstr ""
"裸装……穿这套，\n"
"你就跟没穿一样。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0040_040_0
#. timeline 1476..2187
#: codec/1/166/0xa63e0/1
msgid ""
"The pants are the same as the jungle fatigues.\n"
msgstr ""
"裤子跟丛林迷彩一样。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0040_040_0
#. timeline 2201..3009
#: codec/1/166/0xa63e0/2
msgid ""
"Obviously, since you're exposing your bare skin,\n"
msgstr ""
"毕竟皮肤都露在外面，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0040_040_0
#. timeline 3009..3859
#: codec/1/166/0xa63e0/3
msgid ""
"your defense and camo index are going to be low.\n"
msgstr ""
"防御和迷彩指数都会降低。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0040_040_0
#. timeline 3928..5001
#: codec/1/166/0xa63e0/4
msgid ""
"On the plus side, it's so light you can move around\n"
"quicker.\n"
msgstr ""
"好处是够轻，移动\n"
"更快。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0040_040_0
#. timeline 5335..6102
#: codec/1/166/0xa63e0/5
msgid ""
"Good for showing off muscles, too.\n"
msgstr ""
"也适合秀肌肉。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0040_040_0
#. timeline 6130..6896
#: codec/1/166/0xa63e0/6
msgid ""
"Hey, Snake. I heard they gave you your old code\n"
"name\n"
msgstr ""
"嘿，SNAKE。听说他们给了你\n"
"旧代号\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0040_040_0
#. timeline 6896..7718
#: codec/1/166/0xa63e0/7
msgid ""
"because you used to run around with your shirt\n"
"off. Is that true?\n"
msgstr ""
"因为你以前总光着膀子\n"
"到处跑。真的吗？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0040_040_0
#. timeline 7718..8526
#: codec/1/166/0xa63e0/8
msgid ""
"Don't believe everything you hear. They called me\n"
"\"Naked\"\n"
msgstr ""
"别什么都信。他们叫我\n"
"“裸蛇”\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0040_040_0
#. timeline 8526..9919
#: codec/1/166/0xa63e0/9
msgid ""
"because I went in without gear or food. I had to\n"
"procure everything on site...\n"
msgstr ""
"是因为我不带装备和食物潜入。一切\n"
"都得就地筹措……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0040_040_0
#. timeline 9933..10964
#: codec/1/166/0xa63e0/10
msgid ""
"You mean they sent you into the jungle without\n"
"even a pair of pants?!\n"
msgstr ""
"你是说他们连条裤子都不给你\n"
"就把你扔进丛林？！\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0040_040_0
#. timeline 11020..12483
#: codec/1/166/0xa63e0/11
msgid ""
"On a HALO jump from 35,000 feet?! Sweet Jesus,\n"
"you are a legend!!\n"
msgstr ""
"三万五千英尺\n"
"HALO跳伞？！天，你真是传奇！！\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0040_040_0
#. timeline 12483..13207
#: codec/1/166/0xa63e0/12
msgid ""
"...You're busting my balls, aren't you, Kaz?\n"
msgstr ""
"……你在耍我吧，卡兹？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0040_040_0
#. timeline 13249..13653
#: codec/1/166/0xa63e0/13
msgid ""
"A little bit, yeah.\n"
msgstr ""
"有点，没错。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0040_040_0
#. timeline 13667..14099
#: codec/1/166/0xa63e0/14
msgid ""
"...Hilarious\n"
msgstr ""
"……真好笑\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0060_000_0
#. timeline 445..1393
#: codec/1/166/0xa6910/0
msgid ""
"COoperative OPerationS, or CO-OPS for short,\n"
msgstr ""
"COoperative OPerationS，简称CO-OPS，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0060_000_0
#. timeline 1421..2452
#: codec/1/166/0xa6910/1
msgid ""
"is the term for taking on missions in teams of two\n"
"or more.\n"
msgstr ""
"指以两人以上小队\n"
"执行任务。\n"
